<title>INDIA: Indian exports rose 8.64 percent in May.</title>
<headline>Indian exports rose 8.64 percent in May.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian merchandise exports increased to $2.86 billion in May, up 8.64 percent from $2.63 billion in the same month in 1996, the government said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>    MERCHANDISE TRADE   May 97    Apr 97    May 96</p>
<p>    Exports		  2.86	2.52	2.63</p>
<p>    Imports		  3.21	3.03	3.26</p>
<p>    Trade balance	 -0.35     -0.51     -0.62</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures, in billions of dollars, may not add up due to rounding.  </p>
<p>- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -</p>
<p>Indian merchandise exports fell to $5.40 billion in April and May, down 1.98 percent from $5.51 billion in the same two-month period in 1996, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>    MERCHANDISE TRADE     Apr-May 97	 Apr-May 96</p>
<p>    Exports			5.40		 5.51</p>
<p>    Imports			6.24		 6.28</p>
<p>    Trade balance	     -0.84		-0.77</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures, in billions of dollars, may not add up due to rounding.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
